A.pk=s(["lagaat does arithmetic on numbers YOU type. It does not know your market\u2019s charges, your agent\u2019s rates, or what anything should have cost.",'A blank field prints "not measured". It is never treated as zero. A trip with no home re-weigh gets its cost per kg from the billed weight, and the card says so on that line.',"Landed cost per sellable kg is your total outlay divided by the kilos you can actually sell. If you did not weigh at home and did not count the cull, that figure is the billed-weight figure and is optimistic by however much you lost.","Charges are apportioned across lots by largest remainder, so the shares always sum to exactly the total you typed. An individual lot can differ by \xb11 paisa from charge \xd7 its share.","Each percentage is rounded on its own, so the individual charge percentages need not add up to the total charge percentage exactly; where they differ, they differ by a hundredth. Both are shown, and both name their denominator.","When the total does not tie, that is a prompt to look at the slip again \u2014 not a finding. lagaat cannot tell the difference between a charge you forgot to type, a figure you misread, and anything else. It shows you the working and stops.",'"From memory" mode is a reconstruction. The card is stamped as one. Do not use it as evidence of what a bill said.',"lagaat is not an accounting system, not a dues ledger, and not a legal document. The printed card is a working sheet for your own family.","Local-first: your data is a SQLite file on your machine, the app runs on localhost, nothing syncs anywhere, there are no accounts and no encryption. The demo runs entirely in your browser and stores nothing server-side."],t.s)
